      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like perimenopause, but I'd like to confirm. I'm sending you for a thyroid test because of hot flushes. Let's get a blood count, for irregular periods. I'd like you to take estradiol gel, 1 pump, once a day, long term. It's for menopausal symptoms. Regular exercise, light layers and avoiding triggers can help. Please come and see me in three months.",
